<div id="content">

	<main id="main" role="main" itemscope itemprop="mainContentOfPage" itemtype="http://schema.org/Blog">

		<div id="inner-content" class="wrap cf">

			<div class="m-all t-2of3 d-2of3 cf">

				
						
              
              <article id="post-22079" class="cf post-22079 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-features tag-caravan-safety tag-travel-tips tag-vehicle-theft" role="article" itemscope itemprop="blogPost" itemtype="http://schema.org/BlogPosting">

                <header class="article-header entry-header">

                  <h5 class="single-category"><a href="https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/category/features/" rel="category tag">Features</a></h5>
                
                  <h1 class="entry-title single-title" itemprop="headline" rel="bookmark">Why police-approved caravan security could give owners greater peace of mind</h1>

                  <p class="byline entry-meta vcard author-details">

                    <span class="entry-author author" itemprop="author" itemscope itemptype="http://schema.org/Person">Iain Pemberton</span> | <time class="updated entry-time" datetime="13th July 2026" itemprop="datePublished">13th July 2026</time>
                  </p>

                </header> 
                <div class="single-page-img">
                  <img width="770" height="514" src="https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/rsz_sbd_nemesis_ultra_1.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/rsz_sbd_nemesis_ultra_1.jpg 770w, https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/rsz_sbd_nemesis_ultra_1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/rsz_sbd_nemesis_ultra_1-768x513.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 770px) 100vw, 770px" />                </div>

                <section class="entry-content cf" itemprop="articleBody">
                  <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whether your caravan is parked on your driveway, stored off-site or pitched on a campsite, security is something every owner should take seriously.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">That&#8217;s why the latest announcement from Purple Line, a leading manufacturer of caravan and motorhome security products, is good news for touring enthusiasts. The company has become one of the latest manufacturers to join Secured by Design (SBD), the official police security initiative.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The accreditation recognises several products from Purple Line&#8217;s Fullstop® Security range, including its Excalibur receiver wheel lock, Saracen Gullwing hitch lock, Nemesis Plus wheel lock and Nemesis Ultra wheel lock.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Secured by Design is the only police-backed accreditation scheme for security products in the UK, with approved products meeting recognised standards designed to help deter theft.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As caravans and motorhomes continue to represent a significant investment for many owners, choosing reliable security has become increasingly important.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Purple Line says its accredited products have been developed to combine high levels of protection with simple, everyday usability. Rather than relying on heavy, cumbersome equipment, the wheel and hitch locks are designed to be lightweight, quick to fit and resistant to common methods of attack, including cutting, drilling and freezing.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8220;Our focus has always been on delivering products that combine high-level protection with genuine ease of use,&#8221; explained Jonathan Harrison, managing director at the company.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">&#8220;As theft prevention becomes increasingly important for caravan and motorhome owners, we are proud to offer solutions that are not only highly effective but also simple and practical to use every day,&#8221; he added.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">While no security device can completely eliminate the risk of theft, police-backed products can provide greater peace of mind, particularly when combined with sensible precautions such as secure storage, tracking devices and good campsite security habits.</span></p>
<p><em>Image: Purple Line</em><br style="font-weight: 400;" /><br style="font-weight: 400;" /></p>
                </section> 
                <footer class="article-footer">

                  <h5>Explore Related Content</h5>
                  
                  <p class="tags"><span class="tags-title"></span> <a href="https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/tag/caravan-safety/" rel="tag">caravan safety</a>   |   <a href="https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/tag/travel-tips/" rel="tag">travel tips</a>   |   <a href="https://www.caravantimes.co.uk/tag/vehicle-theft/" rel="tag">vehicle theft</a></p>
                </footer> 
                
              </article> 
					
				
